{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>There is no</b>: He mentioned that the heavens have no mouth, as in \"son of man.\"" "<b>And the meaning of אומר</b>: They are the utterances that have complete meaning, like אומר ראובן, and this will only be from joined words. And the utterance is ראובן, and the voice gives forth the sound of the letter resh of ראובן. And behold, he mentioned that by the sight of the eye of the body and the sight of the eye of the inner soul — wisdom — one will see the truth of the telling of the heavens and what the firmament declares."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:49.248194893Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}